+# AstronomyKit accuracy migration
+
+This migration pins AstronomyKit source revision `c68b96cb87b20a49697af133921b8ad55b7e6ad0`
+(`3.0.0-candidate.1+vsop87b.iau2000b.utc-c72`). It replaces the fixed-obliquity
+planetary observation conversion with the apparent true ecliptic of date.
+Longitude and latitude now come from the same dated vector throughout shared
+chart and fact observations. The dedicated Sun/Moon paths and signed central
+difference speed width are preserved.
+
+The paired production comparison passes all 36 original events, including
+all 12 stations: maximum absolute timing difference 59.477844 seconds.
+Every bracket is at most one second and every angular/station residual meets
+its separate frozen convergence gate. References and tolerances are unchanged.
+`B369-ASTRONOMY-60S` is cleared for this reviewed candidate's local production
+comparison. This does not close #369 or certify complete event-search coverage.
+
+The AstronomyKit `PRODUCTION-INTEGRATION.md` and
+`Scripts/accuracy/results/production/` contain the event table, source/object
+hashes, model/time-table provenance, independent JPL evidence, broader common-TT
+station/position checks, review record and test logs. Review converged in three
+rounds with no outstanding findings. The broader station check covers 2,462
+ordinary Mercury–Saturn roots over 1900–2100, all within 60 seconds.
+
+## Numerical migration
+
+`Date` now has explicit civil UTC semantics; the engine computes planetary
+motion in TT and Earth rotation in modeled UT1. Future civil dates hold the last
+announced leap-second offset. This is not a universal prediction of future UTC
+or Earth orientation. `AstroTime(ut:)` and serialized numeric times remain UT1.
+
+Fact provenance reads the dependency's model identifier. Internal ephemeris
+caches are immutable values scoped to a scan, so no persistent internal cache
+needs rewriting. Consumers must invalidate stored version-dependent results
+and review their changed chart/fact snapshots. Frozen independent event records
+and corpus letters have not been changed to absorb this migration; legacy blind
+calibration and full release evaluation remain separate qualification work.
+
+## Handoff
+
+The dependency is pinned to the exact reviewed, unreleased commit above, using
+the public repository URL. Local verification resolves an immutable checkout
+through a gitignored bare Git mirror because the commit has not been published.
+That mirror is not a consumer dependency. Publish the paired commits before
+asking a clean external checkout to resolve this candidate; no tag or release
+has been published by this migration.
+
+The 137 affected calculation/fact/reference/cache tests, specification validator
+and reference-protocol/manifest checks are recorded alongside the acceptance
+report. Pending-suite reporting remains intact. #369 still owns its certified
+search core, 74-case adapter, legacy integration and complete ElectionEventTests.
+Final macOS debug/release and iOS/tvOS/watchOS builds passed. Linux execution,
+further preselected event/JPL coverage, controlled scan runtime
+and memory qualification remain release work. The initial full-model native
+benchmark is substantially slower; no coefficients were removed to reduce it.
